#
# The Captive Portal's accounting told what the coprocessor carried, put on again at every boot
# while it is wanted (scripts/xgs/cp_overlay.py sync): an OPNsense update that ships the portal's
# file again replaces it, and the pkg trigger os-xgs-npu-cp.ucl does not run for an update that
# was installed while this host was down. Only on the versions of the file it knows.

P=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/cp_overlay.py
[ -x "${P}" ] || exit 0
"${P}" sync > /dev/null 2>&1
exit 0
